  "interpretation": [
    "UDP loss/reordering occurs without SCTP; SCTP fast recovery shrinks the sending window despite queued data and ample receiver window.",
    "TCP/TLS avoids the observed loss amplification. Eight-MiB payloads reach about 3 Mbps through the current proxy; a 512-KiB sample understates bulk capacity.",
    "The native-only WiFi/TLS experiment reaches 7.2-9.5 Mbps; ordinary HTTPS upload also improves from 4.3 to 12.5 Mbps when source-bound to WiFi.",
    "Relay candidates use static protocol preference (UDP above TCP above TLS). The selected allocation retires alternatives, so one profile does not compare their sustained throughput.",
    "Results characterize this network and test setup, not a general preference for TLS, a production speed guarantee, or a proof that the proxy is the only source of loss."
  ],
